    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5051" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμβλ-ωθρίδιον</span></b> , τό,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παιδίον</span>) <i>abortive child,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καὶ ἐκτρώματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.59
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Harp.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Act.
			 (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάρμακον</span>), <i>drug
				to cause abortion,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.7
			</span></i>.—Prop. neut. from <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμβλωθρίδιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
				<i>causing abortion,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aret.
				<u>CA</u>
				2.11
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀμβλώθριον</span></b> , τό, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				137
			</span></i> (s. v.l.).</div>
